I reviewed all of lines 1–96. The file has one bundled structure, `FacePLFilling`, which collects a map with these properties:
- it agrees with the face boundary map on the frontier;
- it is continuous on the region;
- it is injective on the region;
- its image is the closed region of the polygonal circle;
- it is PL on the set;
- it carries a finite PL certificate.

It also has an existence theorem, a `Classical.choice` choice of filling, and a pointwise compatibility lemma.

The structure combines Mathlib predicates (`Set.EqOn`, `ContinuousOn`, `Set.InjOn`, image equality) with project-specific PL notions (`IsPLOnSet`, `FinitePLHomeomorphBetween`). Mathlib has no piecewise-linear manifold or PL-map concept that this structure competes with. It also has no existing bundled "extension of a boundary map that is a homeomorphism onto a region" for these specific data. A bare `Set.EqOn` plus `ContinuousOn` plus `InjOn` bundle is a problem-specific packaging, not a competing concept.

I did not open the PL development in the other files. I saw no sign of a duplicated generic concept in this file.
